1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:07,632
现在，这本书你们肯定都没看过，对吧？
Now, this is definitely not a book I would expect any of you to have ever come across, okay?

2
00:00:07,632 --> 00:00:09,419
作者艾米·莫林，经历特别感人。
Amy Morin, incredibly touching story.

3
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:14,761
我在领英上找到她，发消息聊过，她是个特别棒的生活教练。
I found her on LinkedIn, messaged her, and she’s an incredible life coach.

4
00:00:14,761 --> 00:00:18,979
我最欣赏她的故事，因为特别真实，对吧？
What I really like about her story is it’s personal, okay?

5
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:20,990
我觉得，有个人经历的人那些真正切身经历过的事情，才是你能从中学到东西的。
I think anyone that’s got a personal story

6
00:00:20,990 --> 00:00:22,776
that’s been personally touched—that personal experience—

7
00:00:22,776 --> 00:00:24,116
is something you can learn from.

8
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:30,648
而不是那些没切身实践、没真实经历的人。
that don’t have skin in the game, or that don’t have real-life experiences.

9
00:00:30,648 --> 00:00:32,280
而艾米·莫林绝对有真实经历。
And Amy Morin definitely has it.

10
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,760
如果你读了这本书的简介，就会明白了。
If you read the synopsis of the book, you’ll understand why.

11
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:38,280
她经历过很多残酷的悲剧。
She’s had some real tough tragedies to overcome.

12
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:44,942
但在战胜这些悲剧的过程中，她克服了很多心理弱点。
But in understanding those tragedies she’s had, she’s had to overcome a lot of mental weaknesses.

13
00:00:44,942 --> 00:00:48,719
而正是这些心理弱点，我们大家都有，对吧？
And it’s those mental weaknesses that we all have, okay?

15
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:50,584
没有人能对艾米的经历无动于衷。
None of us are indifferent to Amy.

16
00:00:50,584 --> 00:00:54,868
我们都有这些弱点，在生命的不同时期都会遇到。
We all have these weaknesses. We all come across these weaknesses at various times in our lives.

17
00:00:54,868 --> 00:00:57,640
所以这本书特别值得一读。
And this is why this book is particularly good to read.

18
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:04,260
顺便说一句，她是博主，你还能在YouTube上看她的视频。
Note, obviously, she’s a blogger, so you can obviously watch some YouTube videos of her as well.

20
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:10,308
总结来说，就是要避开我们都容易掉进的心理陷阱，对吧？
In terms of summary, it’s to avoid the mental pitfalls that all of us are prone to, okay?

21
00:01:10,308 --> 00:01:11,899
她在书中特别指出了这些陷阱。
So she highlights those pitfalls.

23
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:13,269
可以说，她在告诉你，她会列出十大常见错误，你很可能会犯这些错，以及这些错误的后果，还有如何克服它们，对吧？
It’s almost like saying, you know,

24
00:01:13,269 --> 00:01:15,139
she’s going to put down the top ten things—

25
00:01:15,139 --> 00:01:17,383
you’re likely to make the mistakes you’re going to make,

26
00:01:17,383 --> 00:01:18,879
and what the outcomes are going to be,

27
00:01:18,879 --> 00:01:20,936
and how you’re going to have to overcome them, okay?

28
00:01:27,409 --> 00:01:29,996
you can identify yourself heading into that pitfall

29
00:01:29,996 --> 00:01:31,936
and avoid getting into it equally.

30
00:01:31,980 --> 00:01:37,820
即使掉进去，也能快速走出来。
If you do fall into one of those weaknesses, You can very quickly get yourself back out.

32
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:42,880
书中几个关键点：自我反思和认知共性。
In terms of, obviously, some of the key highlights: self-reflection and recognition of similarities.

33
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:52,500
还有具体的困境案例和解决方案，理解大多数人会犯的心理错误及如何避免。
Practical examples of hardship and practical solutions. Understanding the mental errors most humans make and how to avoid them.

35
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:55,935
并深入理解这些错误背后的原因。
And then understanding the underlying reasons why they’re occurring.

36
00:01:55,935 --> 00:01:59,989
有时，我们看问题只想解决它，
Sometimes, we tend to look at a problem and just want to solve it,

37
00:01:59,989 --> 00:02:02,594
但你永远找不到真正有效的解决方案除非你先理解问题的根本原因
but you can never really find an effective solution

38
00:02:02,594 --> 00:02:06,937
unless you understand what the underlying cause of the problem was in the first place.

41
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:12,612
当然，说到把无意识的坏习惯转化为有意识的好习惯我们稍后会详细讲解‘从无意识到有意识’的概念
In terms of, obviously, then, transforming unconscious bad habits to conscious smart habits,

42
00:02:12,612 --> 00:02:18,511
we will elaborate on this concept of unconscious to conscious a little bit later on.

43
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:22,839
最后一点，成功人士关注的是什么？
And then the last one, what do successful people focus on?

46
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:28,500
这又回到和蒂姆·费里斯类似的观点——成功人士在做什么
Again, touching on something similar to what Tim Ferriss did—what it is that successful people are doing.

49
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:30,375
他们成功是有原因的
There’s a reason they’re successful.

50
00:02:30,375 --> 00:02:32,555
他们确实有很多共同特质
They all do tend to have some common characteristics.

51
00:02:32,555 --> 00:02:37,399
如果真有这些特质，那我们要确保自己知道是什么，并且去学习
And if they do, we want to make sure we know what they are and ensure that we adopt them.

53
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:42,880
好吧，现在进入练习环节，结束第12单元
Okay, let’s now get on to the drill section and wrap up Unit 12.

54
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:49,870
我一直说，多练才能精通
So, as I always say, practice does make perfect.

55
00:02:50,230 --> 00:02:54,850
这就是练习环节，当然，练习内容都能看到
This is the drill section. Obviously, the drills are available for you to view.

56
00:02:55,130 --> 00:02:58,267
你可以去看练习，完成模板，再回来观看指导教程，做更多笔记，做些调整增增减减
You can go and view that drill, complete your template, come back,

57
00:02:58,267 --> 00:03:01,143
watch the guided tuition, make some more notes, make some adjustments,

58
00:03:01,143 --> 00:03:01,927
add and subtract.

59
00:03:02,450 --> 00:03:06,390
再去看看其他实操案例，继续做笔记
Go watch some of the other practical examples, again, make some notes.

60
00:03:07,410 --> 00:03:12,285
另外，如果你在上课时录屏，我不建议这样做
Equally, if you are recording some of your screens while doing this course, I wouldn't suggest it.

62
00:03:12,285 --> 00:03:15,779
但如果你录了，也别害怕去看这些练习
But if you are, don't be afraid to watch those drills as well.

63
00:03:15,779 --> 00:03:19,004
别害怕在休息日去市场里实操
Don't be afraid to venture into the markets on your days off.

64
00:03:19,004 --> 00:03:22,229
但要记住，你的重点还是完成课程
But do remember, your key focus is to ultimately complete the course.

65
00:03:22,730 --> 00:03:29,510
当然，一旦完成并有信心，就可以开始第13单元了
In terms of that, obviously, once you're done and you're confident, you can then begin the process of starting Unit 13.

68
00:03:30,090 --> 00:03:34,035
培养心理素质，就是要养成别人不愿意做的事。这是句至理名言
Developing mental strength is all about habitually doing the things

69
00:03:34,035 --> 00:03:38,769
that no one else is willing to do. An absolute unique quote.

70
00:03:38,970 --> 00:03:42,997
这话太贴切了，因为很多人不愿意做这些模板
Now, where this is so relevant, not many people want to do these templates.

71
00:03:42,997 --> 00:03:46,161
很多人不愿意整天筛选市场
Not many people want to sift through the markets all day.

72
00:03:46,161 --> 00:03:48,749
很多人不愿意筛选信息
Not many people want to sift through the information.

74
00:03:48,890 --> 00:03:53,216
很多人不愿意打印足迹图并标出所有颜色区域
Not many people want to print off a footprint chart and highlight all the colored areas.

75
00:03:53,216 --> 00:03:55,109
很多人就是不愿意做这些
Not many people want to do that.

77
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:58,308
那你猜怎么着？因为很多人不愿意做
And guess what? Because not many people want to do it,

78
00:03:58,308 --> 00:04:02,669
所以很少有人能发现这个过程中隐藏的机会
not many people are ever going to observe the opportunities that lie within that process.

80
00:04:03,230 --> 00:04:04,765
这就是你的优势所在，对吧？
That's where your edge will come, okay?

81
00:04:04,765 --> 00:04:06,738
去做那些别人不愿意做的事
Do the things that others don't want to do,

82
00:04:09,590 --> 00:04:12,130
祝你好运
Good luck.

83
00:04:12,310 --> 00:04:13,690
第13单元见
I'll see you again in Unit 13.
